WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.381
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.237 --> 00:00:07.820
SPEAKER: In this
video, we'll show you

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.390
how to predict images
using Vertex AI.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:15.050
From Cloud Console,
go to Vertex AI.

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.900
Enable Vertex AI API.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.700
Click Create Dataset.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.030
Select Cloud Storage, and
specify the file path.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.940
The file includes the
list of over 3,000 flowers

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.080
with their names.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.940
Click Train New Model.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:33.440
Specify AutoML and a budget
of 8 maximum node hours.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.820
Start training.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.530
Wait for about an hour.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:37.760
Click Models.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.650
Select the trained model.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.855
Select Deploy and Test tab.

00:00:41.855 --> 00:00:43.760
Click Deploy to Endpoint.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.490
Specify endpoint name, and
allocate one node for it.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:48.950
Click Deploy.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.380
Now, open the
blank presentation.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:55.100
Draw a flower, and create
its screenshot image.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.300
Upload the image.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.820
The image was
predicted as sunflower

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.880
with the confidence of 0.526.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:02.690
That's it.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.750
To learn more about Vertex
AI, look at the links

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.190
in the video description.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:10.540
[MUSIC PLAYING]

